{"id": "EUVD-2026-101134", "enisaUuid": "9306f489-03d2-36b7-9c0b-76f6931b81b9", "description": "CGNS through 4.5.2 contains a stack out-of-bounds read vulnerability in ADFI_read_node_header that allows attackers to crash applications by supplying crafted ADF node headers. Attackers can craft .cgns or .adf files whose non-NUL-terminated end tag causes ADFI_stridx_c to scan past disk_node_data, crashing tools like cgnslist.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T15:01:26", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/cgns-adf-node-header-oob-read", "https://github.com/CGNS/CGNS/blob/3a972d92559787a49c5f9a54974ea1946ecb9d21/src/adf/ADF_internals.c#L6828", "https://github.com/CGNS/CGNS", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/cgns-through-4.5.2-stack-out-of-bounds-read-via-adfi-read-node-header"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110661", "GHSA-c64r-37fg-rgvp"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5d40fe7e-1dc3-34a7-aaca-efe21c4bc6e2", "product": {"name": "CGNS", "vendor": {"name": "CGNS"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22644.5.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b5cd86f3-3709-382e-956f-cec3c5e0589a", "vendor": {"name": "CGNS"}}], "isExploited": false}